STEP 1 — Add the required-components set and component payload to the CU model.
File: src/main/scala/itrcompiler/domain/models/CU.scala
- Add field `components: Map[String, String] = Map.empty` to the `CU` case
  class. Keys are exactly: coordinates, requirements, implementation-steps,
  acceptance. Default empty = backward compatible with old batches.
- Add to `object CU`:
  `val requiredComponents: Set[String] = Set("coordinates", "requirements", "implementation-steps", "acceptance")`
  `val componentFileNames: Map[String, String] = Map("coordinates" -> "COORDINATES.itr", "requirements" -> "REQUIREMENTS.itr", "implementation-steps" -> "IMPLEMENTATION_STEPS.itr", "acceptance" -> "ACCEPTANCE.itr")`
- Add method to `CU`:
  `def missingComponents: Set[String] = CU.requiredComponents -- components.keySet`
- Do NOT touch `fileName`, `isRequiredPart`, `CUType`, or `requiredParts`.
  ARCH/LEGEND file names stay exactly as they are.

STEP 2 — Add the batch synopsis model.
New file: src/main/scala/itrcompiler/domain/models/CUSynopsis.scala
```scala
package itrcompiler.domain.models

final case class CUSynopsis(
  features: Seq[String] = Seq.empty,
  maxAttempts: Int = 3,
  summary: String = ""
) extends Model {
  def isComplete: Boolean = features.nonEmpty && summary.trim.nonEmpty
}
```
Default maxAttempts=3 matches SYNOPSIS.itr of feat-1. `isComplete` is false
when the summary is missing or blank — the validator (cu-002) relies on it.

STEP 3 — Attach synopsis to the batch.
File: src/main/scala/itrcompiler/domain/models/CUBatch.scala
- Change to `final case class CUBatch(cus: Seq[CU], synopsis: Option[CUSynopsis] = None)`.
- Grep for every `CUBatch(` call site (main + test) and confirm each still
  compiles — the default keeps all existing call sites source-compatible.

